(pass) allows failed/cancelled runs only when no attempted side effects are recorded
(pass) blocks a succeeded action even when the run failed afterwards
(pass) blocks uncertain remote outcomes and attempts that are marked failed
(pass) missing/truncated history never becomes proof of no side effects
(pass) ambiguous receipt errors stay blocked even without an action mirror
(pass) successful, active and unknown run states are not retried under a failure label
(pass) unknown attempt counters or action states fail closed

